cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below,
  and cite the accompanying paper using the preferred-citation entry.
title: >-
  Accidental accuracy and vertex corrections in GW: Exact benchmarks for the extended Hubbard model
abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebook implementing exact diagonalization (ED) and
  model-space static GW / COHSEX theory for the half-filled extended
  Hubbard ring, used to benchmark the GW approximation and extract the
  effective vertex Gamma_eff(U,V) against the numerically exact gap.
  Reproduces every figure and table in the accompanying paper, including
  the N=6, 10, 14 finite-size scaling of the accidental-cancellation
  point U*(N).
type: software
